# MEGALIGHTS-NORT: Shadows Stochastic (MegaLights: ReSTIR DI samples, one visibility test each) on a device WITHOUT ray query. The method is no longer lowered for want of rays; its visibility source is (Common::Scalability::StochasticVisibility): rayquery -> vsm+screen (the screen trace over the closest HZB, then the light's VSM-LOCAL pages) -> screen. machine.json HideRayTracing=true hides the ray query; the device still has fragment stores and the 16k render area, so the source is vsm+screen.
# Headless shots, F:/BistroFoliageProj, machine.json {"HideRayTracing": true}, Shadows.Method Stochastic (3) overridden in machine.json.
Дано: F:/BistroFoliageProj, GI_Bistro_Night, machine.json HideRayTracing=true, Lit, camera on the street under the lamps.
Когда: run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Stochastic"; render 120 frames; state render,log
Тогда [megalights_nort] 0_night_stochastic_nort: state render.shadows.method == "Stochastic" (requested Stochastic, NOT lowered to CascadedMaps; no "[RenderMethods] Shadows:" lowering line in engine_log), render.shadows.visibility == "vsm+screen"; 0 VUID in engine_log; no "MegaLights:" error line except the one-time "MegaLights: Volume has no vsm+screen visibility yet" (step 2); every local light casts a shadow: each lamp's pool on the pavement has the shadow of the poles/chairs/tables in it (pixel-diff against a Shadows.Method VirtualMaps shot of the same camera: the shadow shapes coincide), and the frame mean is not black (frame mean > the VirtualMaps shot's mean * 0.8).
Когда: run Quality "Quality: Shadows.Method Level"
Тогда 1_level override removed (machine.json clean of Shadows.Method).
